      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>The chicken liver sponge has sailed through a test of its ability to filter pollutants in a harbour in Spain’s Costa Brava</p><p>In the polluted waters of Marina Palamós on Spain’s Costa Brava, Manuel Maldonado, a sponge biologist, noticed something unusual last month: red starfish had started settling in the area.</p><p>Nearly two years earlier, the Spanish National Research Council scientist and his colleagues had begun <a href=\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2026.1875098/full\">transplanting sea sponges</a> into the port to study whether they could survive in its polluted waters.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/01/sea-chicken-liver-sponge-filter-pollutants-harbour-spain-costa-brava\">Continue reading...</a>"
